 "bloques": [
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Greet and say the name",
   "texto": [
    "Hei, it's the most common greeting. Hallo! is also used, for example, when answering the phone. God dag is a somewhat more formal greeting.",
    "Ha det! It's good to say goodbye. Tak is «Thank you.» and ja / nei are «yes / no».",
    "To introduce you: Jeg heter Anna («My name is Anna.»). To ask: Hva heter du? («What's your name?»). The verb heter does not change between jeg and du, unlike «my name / your name» in Spanish."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "A nice phrase.",
   "texto": [
    "Hyggelig å hilse på deg equals «Encantado de saludarte / conocerte». Hyggelig literally means «Nice.», but this greeting does not translate word for word. It marks the infinitive, such as «-ar/-er» or «a» in some constructions."
   ]
  },
