 "intro": "In written bokmål, hei serves both by greeting someone known and someone you just met. In Norwegian it is used in a regular way even with unknown; there is no daily opposition equivalent to you / you. It does exist, but today it sounds very formal or old-fashioned in many situations. The pronouncements are close to the eastern talk of Norway; there is variation between dialects."
